<http://data.silknow.org/object/f1b9f98f-aaf2-32da-9be6-757ddb456ded>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Plain weave cotton embroidered with silk in straight stitches and pulled thread work; whitework.\nDisplayed behind glass.\nThere is a square of embroidery in each corner in the form of a square grid composed of pairs of diagonal lozenges in straight stitch.  The border between these has 6 or 7 hexagons of pulled thread work creating holes; between the hexagons are converging diagonal lines of straight stitch forming triangles containing 4 small triangles forming a stepped flower and a pair of leaves. Above this border is a narrow band of zigzagging lozenges.  This also appears below the border where it is edged with a line of crosses.\nThe pulled thread ground of the hexagons in repeated in the large central rectangular panel and in the irregularly shaped corner units from which a thick point extends into the field.  It is also in the small diamond on a triangular base and stem which extends from mid-way along each side.  All these elements are edged with reciprocal diamond-heads. The central and corner units have an additional inner border of reciprocal triangles on a pulled thread ground."@en , "embroidered, 1700s, Persian; Whitework"@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/f38f4fd0-6217-3afb-ba70-a9e025286f94> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Plain weave cotton embroidered with silk in straight stitches and pulled thread work; whitework.\nDisplayed behind glass.\nThere is a square of embroidery in each corner in the form of a square grid composed of pairs of diagonal lozenges in straight stitch.  The border between these has 6 or 7 hexagons of pulled thread work creating holes; between the hexagons are converging diagonal lines of straight stitch forming triangles containing 4 small triangles forming a stepped flower and a pair of leaves. Above this border is a narrow band of zigzagging lozenges.  This also appears below the border where it is edged with a line of crosses.\nThe pulled thread ground of the hexagons in repeated in the large central rectangular panel and in the irregularly shaped corner units from which a thick point extends into the field.  It is also in the small diamond on a triangular base and stem which extends from mid-way along each side.  All these elements are edged with reciprocal diamond-heads. The central and corner units have an additional inner border of reciprocal triangles on a pulled thread ground."@en , "embroidered, 1700s, Persian; Whitework"@en ;
        ecrm:P43_has_dimension         <http://data.silknow.org/object/f1b9f98f-aaf2-32da-9be6-757ddb456ded/dimension/1> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/f1b9f98f-aaf2-32da-9be6-757ddb456ded/dimension/2> ;
        dc:identifier                  "933-1889" ;
        <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs>
                <https://collections.vam.ac.uk/item/O158530> .

