<http://data.silknow.org/object/f1b9f98f-aaf2-32da-9be6-757ddb456ded/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Plain weave cotton embroidered with silk in straight stitches and pulled thread work; whitework.\nDisplayed behind glass.\nThere is a square of embroidery in each corner in the form of a square grid composed of pairs of diagonal lozenges in straight stitch.  The border between these has 6 or 7 hexagons of pulled thread work creating holes; between the hexagons are converging diagonal lines of straight stitch forming triangles containing 4 small triangles forming a stepped flower and a pair of leaves. Above this border is a narrow band of zigzagging lozenges.  This also appears below the border where it is edged with a line of crosses.\nThe pulled thread ground of the hexagons in repeated in the large central rectangular panel and in the irregularly shaped corner units from which a thick point extends into the field.  It is also in the small diamond on a triangular base and stem which extends from mid-way along each side.  All these elements are edged with reciprocal diamond-heads. The central and corner units have an additional inner border of reciprocal triangles on a pulled thread ground."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/f1b9f98f-aaf2-32da-9be6-757ddb456ded> .
